# Images

Never copy a PNG, JPEG, GIF, or Canva export into the repo. Every raster goes through `npm run optimize:images` first. Read `.cursor/skills/optimize-images/SKILL.md` when adding or replacing an image.

```bash
npm run optimize:images -- /path/to/source --name slug --kind logo|graphic|photo
npm run check:media
```

- Output is **WebP only**, in `public/images/`. No originals beside it.
- **logo** — UI marks. Lossless, max edge 512.
- **graphic** — intro frames, type on transparent. Lossless, max edge 2560.
- **photo** — camera/Canva photos. Lossy q80–90, max edge 2560 (2× of `max-w-7xl`).
- Pass `--max-width` at **2× CSS display** (3× if the mark is under ~80px tall).
- Keep SVG as SVG. Do not rasterize it.

## Critical (intro, LCP, above the fold)

1. Preload the exact URL in `index.html` (`as="image"`, `fetchpriority="high"` for the first frame).
2. `await decodeImages([url])` before adding the class that starts CSS animation.
3. Set `width` / `height` on `<img>` to the optimizer’s printed pixels. First frame: `fetchPriority="high"` `decoding="sync"`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — animation starts while a raw PNG is still on the network
<img className="intro-seq intro-seq-1" src="/images/logo.png" alt="" />

// ✅ GOOD — optimized WebP, preloaded, animation waits on decode
<img src={first.src} width={first.width} height={first.height} fetchPriority="high" decoding="sync" alt="" />
```

## Everything else

- `loading="lazy"` `decoding="async"` plus `width` / `height`.
- Markdown images still get dimensions when wired as a real `<img>`.

`npm run build` runs `check:media` (rejects raw rasters, oversized files, missing preloads).
